# ⭐ THE SIX MARKETING PATHS (added 2026-09-12). These are what make the site
# more than one page to a search engine. Each section used to be reachable only
# as a hash route (#/faq), and a fragment is not a page: the whole site was the
# single URL https://highlightingutah.com/. With these rewrites /faq is a real
# address that Netlify answers, and the router reads it from location.pathname.
#
# ⚠ THEY ARE LISTED ONE BY ONE RATHER THAN AS /* ON PURPOSE. A catch-all would
# answer 200 to every mistyped address on the domain, so every typo becomes a
# page serving the homepage — a soft 404, which Google treats as a quality
# problem and which hides real broken links from us as well. An unknown path
# SHOULD 404, so only the routes that exist are listed.
#
# ⚠ AND THEY ARE THE SAME LIST AS PATH_ROUTES IN index.html AND THE <loc>s IN
# sitemap.xml. A path in the sitemap with no rewrite here is a 404 we asked
# Google to crawl. search-visibility.test.js compares all three and fails if
# they drift; add a route and add it in every one.
/how-it-works  /index.html  200
/gallery       /index.html  200
/reviews       /index.html  200
/areas         /index.html  200
/faq           /index.html  200
/contact       /index.html  200
/privacy       /index.html  200

# /home forces the real homepage past the saved-login redirect — for staff
# checking the site, not customers who want to land on their pending item.
/home  /index.html  200

# The customer token links. The token in the path IS the credential, which is
# why robots.txt Disallows all three.
/q/*  /index.html  200
/r/*  /index.html  200
/s/*  /index.html  200
